/*!
\module QDocTest
\title External Link Tests

We have defined external pages for "RFC 6749", "RFC6749 -", "åøæ", "小部件"
and "---".

\l{RFC 6749} should go to \c{https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749}

\l{RFC 6749 -} should go to \c{https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6749#section-1.3.1}

A link like this should work: \l{RFC 6749-}

A link like this should fail if used: \l{-RFC 6749}{\\l{-RFC 6749}}

\l{åøæ}

\l{小部件}

\l{---}

//! Note that we can't write \l{}{\\l{}} here because QDoc stops parsing the
//! link command after the empty braces and therefore doesn't treat the second
//! set of braces as a second optional argument to the command:

An empty link will fail if used: \l{} \\l{}
*/
